 es
DESCRIPTION:Loneliness is a public health epidemic\, and housing is a powe
 rful\, often overlooked lever for addressing it\, shaping who we connect w
 ith and whether we feel embedded in community. This session explores how d
 ifferent housing models can rebuild social connection\, while confronting 
 the mental health toll of isolation and the barriers facing unhoused older
  adults. Speakers Paula Carder - Director\, Institute on Aging\, Portland 
 State University Samar Jha - Government Affairs Director\, AARP Sheila Jon
 es - Chief for Adult Protective Services\, Family Services Administration
 \, DC DHS Nancy Kelly - Charter member\, Village Hearth Cohousing Laurie T
