DESCRIPTION:Hear from GW Engineering alumnus Saquib Saifee \, M.S. '23\, S
 ecurity Engineer at IBM\, CISSP\, eCPPT\, at BSides Northern Virginia in A
 rlington\, VA! On October 31\, he will present "MCP Servers Are a New Atta
 ck Surface: How to Securely Build and Use Them" to an engaged audience of 
 security engineers and AI practitioners. Model Context Protocol (MCP) is o
 nly as secure as the server you build it on. In under two years\, it has b
 ecome the standard integration layer connecting AI agents to enterprise sy
 stems\, databases\, source code\, and production APIs. However\, an agent 
 crosses a trust boundary on every tool call and resource fetch\, and the p
 rotocol leaves the server to decide what is allowed. If the\nCategory: Lec
