CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Kunqu\, a 600-year-old form of Chinese opera known for its poe
 tic lyrics and refined singing\, was among the first Chinese art forms UNE
 SCO recognized as a "Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Hu
 manity" in 2001. The story of how Kunqu survived the political upheavals o
 f the twentieth century runs not only through state-sponsored troupes in C
 hina but also through communities of devoted amateur singers\, known as qu
 you (曲友)\, who carried the tradition to Taiwan. This talk follows thes
 e enthusiasts from their roots in Mainland China to their postwar lives in
  Taiwan\, where they kept Kunqu alive through informal singing gatherings 
 long before it was celebrated as world heritage. When c\nCategory: Arts & 
 Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/humanities-in-as
 ia-going-beyond-make-do-the-reshaping-of-a-chinese-operatic-tradition-in-t
 aiwan
