DESCRIPTION:A multidisciplinary showcase from the artists and scholars of 
 the full-time faculty and staff at the Corcoran School of the Arts & Desig
 n. A Gift In Motion loosely draws from Robin Wall Kimmerer’s book The Se
 rviceberry which uplifts Indigenous frameworks of the natural world to adv
 ance the possibilities in collectivity\, reciprocity\, and the mindset of 
 abundance. These are anti-capitalist models and theories that provide insi
 ght into the systems of power we negotiate\, but also offer a lens on how 
 we individually move through our daily lives—together—through historic
 ally fraught landscapes. A keen reminder that working with\, for\, and bec
 ause of each other remains the most human motivation\, eve\nCategory: Arts
